-------------------------------
Signals (Angular 16 and Above)
-------------------------------
Option 1: zone.js is a library (Angular 2) that helps Angular know when 
          something has changed so it can automatically update the UI.
        
                    Button Click / HTTP Response / Timer
                                    ↓
                                 Zone.js
                                    ↓
                          Angular Change Detection
                                    ↓
                           Checks component tree


Option 2: Think of a signal as a variable that Angular automatically tracks.
          When the signal value changes, Angular knows exactly what needs to be 
          updated in the UI.

                        count signal changed
                                ↓
           Angular knows which component/template uses count
                                ↓
                   Updates only that part of the UI

In the context of UI updates and change detection, Signals are generally more
efficient than the traditional Zone.js-based approach.


Signals
   ├── signal()
   ├── Reading a signal
   ├── set()
   ├── update()
   ├── computed()
   └── effect()


/*------------------------ with signal-------------------- */
user.ts
----------
import { Component,signal,computed } from '@angular/core';

const randomIndex = Math.floor(Math.random() * DUMMY_USERS.length);

export class UserComponent {
  selectedUser=signal(DUMMY_USERS[randomIndex]); // reactive state

  onSelectedUser(){
    const randomIndex = Math.floor(Math.random() * DUMMY_USERS.length);
    this.selectedUser.set(DUMMY_USERS[randomIndex]);
  }

  imagePath=computed(()=> 'users/' + this.selectedUser().avatar);
}

user.html
---------
<div>
    <button (click)="onSelectedUser()">     <!-- Event Binding -->
        <img 
            [src]="imagePath()"
            [alt]="selectedUser().name"
        />
        <span>{{ selectedUser().name }}</span>
    </button>
</div>



